// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// TIER INTEGRITY — the declared above-tier residency exceptions (sc-15799)
//
// THE INVARIANT (normative statement: `docs/memory-strategy-contract.md`, "Tier integrity"):
//
//     No component is resident above the user's selected quant tier unless a DECLARED, MEASURED
//     exception says otherwise.
//
// Choosing q8 or q4 *is* a memory decision. If a user picks q4 because bf16 does not fit, carrying any
// component at bf16 defeats the choice they made. This file is the catalog's answer to "which components
// sit above the selected tier, on which tiers, and at what cost" — the audit sc-15799 demanded.
// `scripts/check-tier-integrity.mjs` validates it, generates `docs/generated/tier-integrity.md` from it,
// and fails `npm run check` (and with it the parity lane) on drift.
//
// IS IT COMPLETE? It is complete AGAINST THE THRESHOLD BELOW, which is not the same thing as complete.
// The first revision of this file claimed completeness outright; a review then found three omissions
// whose costs were already sitting in the tree (5 mage `transformerHead` rows, `krea_2_raw`'s VAE, and
// all twelve SenseNova-U1 (model, component) pairs). That is what an unstated threshold buys you, so
// here it is. A SECOND review then found the SenseNova pairs mis-declared rather than merely missing —
// they claimed bf16 on both lanes when candle-gen holds them at f32 — so those twelve pairs are now
// twenty-four ROWS, one per lane. The amnesty is keyed per PAIR, so it is still twelve slots.
//
// THE THRESHOLD — what must be declared, and what must not.
//   DECLARE: any component this ledger's vocabulary names (textEncoder / vae / visionTower /
//     controlBranch / identityAdapters / transformerHead) that a provider holds above the selected tier,
//     AT ANY SIZE. Size is deliberately not a filter: `mage_flow_base` / `transformerHead` is 0.009 GB
//     and is declared, because the point of the row is that a "q4" render is partly q8 — not that it is
//     big. A component is declarable if some packing path in the tree could in principle target it: a
//     stack of `[out, in]` Linears, or a conv stack a provider packs elsewhere.
//   DO NOT DECLARE: per-channel and per-token VECTORS — RMSNorm / LayerNorm / QK-norm scales, modulation
//     and bias vectors, timestep and noise-scale embedders. No packer in the tree targets these at any
//     tier for any model, so they are not above-tier CHOICES; declaring them would add a near-identical
//     row to every entry in the catalog and drown the rows that record a decision.
//   ALSO OUT OF SCOPE: activation transients and workspace (this is a residency ledger, not a peak
//     ledger), and BELOW-tier residency, which the invariant permits outright — it is one-directional.
// A reader who finds an above-tier component on the DECLARE side with no row here has found an omission,
// not an exercise of judgment. File it.
//
// WHAT THE AUDIT FOUND, stated plainly: above-tier residency is NOT rare. On a q4 or q8 tier the great
// majority of image entries keep a VAE, a text encoder, or both resident at f16, bf16, or f32. The story that
// opened this expected a handful; the honest count is most of the catalog. That is why this file exists
// as a ledger rather than a footnote — and why every row carries an in-tree citation for the FACT even
// where the COST is not yet measured.
//
// ROW SHAPE
//   model            catalog entry id in config/manifests/builtin.models.jsonc
//   component        which component is above tier (textEncoder / vae / visionTower / controlBranch /
//                    identityAdapters / transformerHead)
//   residentTier     the precision it is actually resident at: "f32" | "bf16" | "q8". PER LANE — see
//                    `backends`. Where a component's residency differs between the two ports, this is
//                    the value for the lanes THIS row claims, not a compromise across both.
//   appliesToTiers   the SELECTED tiers on which it is above tier (never includes a tier at or below
//                    residentTier — the checker enforces this)
//   backends         which lanes carry it: ["mlx"], ["candle"], or both. REQUIRED — never defaulted.
//                    THE SAME DECLARED TIER CAN YIELD DIFFERENT RESIDENCY PER BACKEND — that is a
//                    tier-integrity fact in its own right, because the two ports make independent dtype
//                    decisions. `sensenova_u1_8b`'s vision conv kernels and `fm_head` are bf16 under
//                    mlx-gen but f32 under candle-gen, which widens every dense leaf it multiplies
//                    against an f32 activation (`candle-gen-sensenova/src/quant.rs::get_f32`, sc-14249);
//                    the `mage_flow*` transformerHead q8 floor is declared by both providers, so the
//                    q4 component profile is backend-invariant. A differing component is declared as ONE ROW
//                    PER LANE: the checker's uniqueness key is (model, component, LANE), so two rows may
//                    split the lanes but never claim the same one.
//                    This field is ENFORCED, not advisory: lane names are validated, every declared
//                    lane must be one the ROUTER serves the model on, and the lane is published as a
//                    column in docs/generated/tier-integrity.md. It was an unvalidated passthrough that
//                    the generated audit dropped until the sc-15799 review.
//
//                    WHY IT IS MANDATORY (sc-17395). sc-15799 left the key optional, with omission
//                    meaning "both" — and the lane cross-check ran only when the key was PRESENT, so
//                    the defaulted claim was the one nothing validated. Every model in this ledger is
//                    routed on BOTH lanes, so all 42 omitting rows were asserting that their
//                    residentTier and cost hold identically under two independently-written loaders.
//                    Nobody had checked the second one. That is not a hypothetical: it is how the six
//                    chroma rows carried candle's f32 figure on the mlx lane (sc-16462, 2x), and it is
//                    what the twelve SenseNova pairs got wrong before they were split into 24 rows.
//                    Spelling the lanes is how a row states which loader its number was read from.
//
//                    THE LANE ORACLE IS THE ROUTER, NOT THE MANIFEST. A manifest `mlx`/`candle` block
//                    is optional per-backend TUNING config (vramGbByTier, minMemoryGb) — only 44 of 86
//                    entries carry a `candle` block, while `anima_base` has none and is generated by
//                    the registered `candle-gen-anima`. Reading block presence as lane existence is
//                    what let sc-16462 conclude chroma had no candle lane and delete a live f32 fact.
//   cause            "packing-exception"   a deliberate quality decision: this component is not packed
//                                          because packing it measurably or structurally hurts.
//                    "backend-capability"  the backend cannot serve the on-disk format, so it upcasts.
//                                          Packing cannot fix this; a compute path or a re-host can.
//                    "structural"          there is nothing quantizable (all-conv, folded-away leaves).
//   reason           one sentence, in the terms the provider itself uses.
//   evidence.state   always "measured". `costGb` / `costBytes` are legacy scalar evidence;
//                    `costBytesByTier` records an exact isolated cost for every applicable tier.
//   evidence.source  file:line where the fact (and the number, when measured) is recorded in-tree.
//   evidence.isolation how the component was separated from bundled totals.
//   evidence.triageDecision / reviewedCause / triageNote record the eliminate-vs-measure decision and
//                    the cause re-check performed while measuring the former sc-15799 debt.
//
// A NOTE ON HONESTY. sc-16015 measures the formerly-unmeasured rows from immutable safetensors headers:
// exact tensor shapes are counted at each backend's runtime load dtype. This isolates weight residency
// without borrowing from per-tier totals, whole-model peaks, activation transients, or allocator floors.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
{
  "$schema": "../packages/schemas/tier-integrity.schema.json",
  // sc-16015 emptied the temporary sc-15799 measurement amnesty. The checker now rejects every
  // `unmeasured` exception unconditionally.
  "exceptions": [
    // ── The declared quality carve-out this story ratified ───────────────────────────────────────────
    {
      "model": "krea_2_turbo",
      "component": "controlBranch",
      "residentTier": "q8",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4"],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "Packing the pose-control branch to q4 measures \"pose-locked; non-pose details drift\" — the control residual is precision-sensitive (RMS-clamped at τ) and is the thing the user actually asked for, so a q4 base floors its branch at q8 instead of following the tier down.",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costGb": 1.6,
        "source": "crates/media/candle-gen/candle-gen-krea/src/control.rs `ControlBranch::from_checkpoint_quantized` — \"the ~6.6 GB dense branch never lands in VRAM, and the resident footprint is ~1.7 GB at q4 / ~3.3 GB at q8\"; the q8 floor forgoes the 3.3 − 1.7 = 1.6 GB difference.",
        "note": "The q8 case is NOT an exception: on a q8 base the branch follows the tier exactly, which is why sc-15799 deleted the branch-quant lever outright rather than keeping its q8 rung. RETRACTION (sc-15799 review): this row first cited `candle.control.branchPackSaveGb` (q8 −8.4 / q4 −10.2 GB) for a costGb of 1.8. Both figures exceed the ENTIRE 6.6 GB branch, so neither can be a weight-side quantity; the manifest key is deleted and the worker applies no correction. SC-16013 replaced the stale peaks with direct measurements against the packed branches that ship. NOTE ALSO what the deleted lever gave up on the q8 tier: it could pack a q8 base's branch to q4, one tier BELOW the selection, which tier integrity permits — see the capability-loss note on `candle.control.branchTierByBaseTier` in the manifest and the \"What tier integrity gives up\" section of docs/memory-strategy-contract.md."
      },
      "backends": [
        "mlx",
        "candle"
      ]
    },

    // ── Lens text encoder: resolved, so deliberately NO exception row (sc-16014) ────────────────────
