      "reason": "resolve_quant packs ONLY the transformer, and candle-gen-chroma additionally loads the dense T5-XXL into f32 containers \u2014 its stated rationale is f32 DiT activations and mlx parity, though the transformer casts at the call site regardless, so the width is a load-time choice rather than a hard requirement.",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costBytesByTier": {
          "q4": 19049242624,
          "q8": 19049242624
        },
        "source": "crates/media/candle-gen/candle-gen-chroma/src/text.rs::load_t5 — \"Load the T5-XXL encoder from the Chroma snapshot's `text_encoder/` ..., at f32 on `device`\", via `candle_gen::mmap_var_builder(&files, DType::F32, device)`; isolated artifact: SceneWorks/chroma1-hd-mlx@9d99afe1ebca67032476756bc70d4a7152bc1bd5:q8/text_encoder/model-00001-of-00002.safetensors, q8/text_encoder/model-00002-of-00002.safetensors",
        "isolation": "Summed the exact safetensors-header tensor byte spans for q8/text_encoder/model-00001-of-00002.safetensors + q8/text_encoder/model-00002-of-00002.safetensors at immutable revision 9d99afe1ebca67032476756bc70d4a7152bc1bd5; all 219 tensors are BF16 on disk, but the candle lane materializes them at the F32 runtime load dtype (its own comment: \"loading the bf16 checkpoint as f32 keeps the weight values (bf16) in f32 containers\"), so floating tensors are counted at 4 bytes for THIS lane while the mlx sibling counts 2. The element counts are the same artifact's and are shared with that row. This is isolated weight residency, excluding activations and allocator overhead.",
        "triageDecision": "measure",
        "reviewedCause": "packing-exception",
        "triageNote": "Measure, not eliminate: unlike the mlx sibling — whose bf16 residency an on-device repack could remove (sc-16462) — this row's extra width is a deliberate load-dtype decision at the candle load site, tied to the f32 DiT activations and mlx parity (the transformer casts at the call site regardless). Eliminating it means changing the candle compute dtype, not repacking an artifact, and that is a CUDA-lane change tracked as sc-17439.",
        "note": "RESTORED by sc-17395. sc-16462 correctly halved the mlx figure (the T5/VAE are bf16 on disk and mlx-gen loads them at that native width, not f32) but then deleted the f32 fact entirely, on the premise that \"the catalog hosts no `candle` block for any chroma entry, so that residency is unreachable\". A manifest per-backend block is optional tuning config, not a lane declaration: chroma1_* is `candle_routed: true` in crates/sceneworks-core/src/jobs_store/routing/catalog.rs and `candle_gen_chroma::register_providers` is wired at candle-gen-catalog/src/lib.rs, so the candle lane ships. The f32 residency is therefore REACHABLE and was undeclared between sc-16462 and sc-17395 — the exact defect the invariant forbids. Split per lane on the SenseNova precedent rather than dropped: declaring bf16 for both would under-declare candle, f32 for both would over-declare mlx (which is what sc-16462 found). See the mlx sibling row."
      },
      "backends": [
        "candle"
      ]
