    // ── Within-tier precision floors: a "q4" tier that is partly q8 ──────────────────────────────────
    // These are the sharpest cases in the ledger. The user selects q4 and gets q8 weights for part of
    // the model. `precisionFloors` and each provider descriptor now make the substitution readable by
    // the worker's tier resolver, asset telemetry, UI and memory-evidence identity (sc-16025).
    {
      "model": "mage_flow_base",
      "component": "textEncoder",
      "residentTier": "q8",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4"],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "An 8-bit FLOOR on the Qwen3-VL LM's 36 decoder layers: a q4 request is silently raised to 8 bits for them, so the q4 tier shares q8's decoder layers and differs only in the token embedding and the vision tower.",
