    // ── SenseNova-U1: a unified model whose dense heads the first audit missed ────────────────────────
    // All six entries host q4/q8/bf16, and BOTH lanes state that the token embedding, `lm_head`, the
    // flow-matching head and the vision embedders stay dense in every tier. There is no separate VAE or
    // text encoder to declare on this family, which is exactly how it fell through the first pass.
    //
    // ONE ROW PER LANE (second sc-15799 review). The lanes hold these components at DIFFERENT
    // precisions: mlx-gen keeps them at the checkpoint's bf16 store dtype, while candle-gen widens the
    // two vision conv kernels and `fm_head` to **f32** (`candle-gen-sensenova/src/quant.rs::get_f32`,
    // sc-14249) so every dense leaf it multiplies against an f32 activation shares one dtype. A single
    // both-lanes row could only be wrong in one direction or the other, so the checker's uniqueness key
    // is (model, component, lane) and each lane declares its own `residentTier`. sc-16015 measures each
    // lane separately at that runtime dtype.
    {
      "model": "sensenova_u1_8b",
      "component": "transformerHead",
      "residentTier": "bf16",
      "appliesToTiers": [
        "q4",
        "q8"
      ],
      "backends": [
        "mlx"
      ],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "The Qwen3 backbone is packed but the token embedding, `lm_head` and the flow-matching `fm_head` stay dense bf16 in every tier under mlx-gen — the tier author's split, which the packer follows rather than overrides. (the base entry.)",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costBytesByTier": {
          "q4": 2548054016,
          "q8": 2548054016
        },
        "source": "crates/media/mlx-gen/mlx-gen-sensenova/src/convert.rs — \"a 2-D dense target (`embed_tokens` / `lm_head` / `fm_head`) is never packed\"; crates/media/mlx-gen/mlx-gen-sensenova/src/quant.rs — \"Everything else stays dense in every tier: the token embedding, `lm_head`, ... the flow-matching `fm_head`, and the timestep/noise-scale embedders\". MLX holds them at the checkpoint's bf16 store dtype; it does not widen (the only f32 in the MLX vision path is a transient positional-embedding cast that is immediately cast back to the input dtype).; isolated artifact: SceneWorks/sensenova-u1-8b-mlx@b6206ea2e888198418b92f3bed31f5506c6183f9:q8/model.safetensors#{language_model.model.embed_tokens,language_model.lm_head,fm_modules.fm_head}.*",
        "isolation": "Summed the exact safetensors-header tensor shapes for q8/model.safetensors#{language_model.model.embed_tokens,language_model.lm_head,fm_modules.fm_head}.* at immutable revision b6206ea2e888198418b92f3bed31f5506c6183f9; floating tensors were counted at the BF16 runtime load dtype for the mlx lane, while integer metadata tensors retained their native width. This is isolated weight residency, excluding activations and allocator overhead.",
        "triageDecision": "measure",
        "reviewedCause": "packing-exception",
        "triageNote": "Measure, not eliminate: the provider deliberately excludes this component from packing, and the tree contains no verified quality-neutral lower-tier artifact that could replace it before calibration.",
        "note": "ADDED by the sc-15799 review, which found all six SenseNova-U1 entries undeclared. ADJUDICATION: U1 is a unified MoT model with \"no separate VAE or text encoder\", so the ledger's diffusion vocabulary does not map cleanly — but that is a naming problem, not a reason to omit. The dense matmul targets ARE declarable under this file's threshold (they are `[out, in]` Linears a packer could take, and the packer deliberately skips them), so they are declared: `transformerHead` for `embed_tokens` / `lm_head` / `fm_head`, `visionTower` for the two Conv vision embedders. The dense RMSNorms, QK-norms and timestep/noise-scale embedders are NOT declared — they are per-channel vectors, which the threshold excludes for every model. MEASURED by sc-16015 from the exact selected tensor shapes in each immutable q8 safetensors header, counted at the lane-specific runtime dtype; no whole-model figure or shape estimate is borrowed. SPLIT PER LANE by the second sc-15799 review, which found the single both-lanes row UNDER-DECLARED candle. The two ports make independent dtype decisions and the ledger's uniqueness key is now (model, component, lane), so each lane states its own residentTier instead of one of them being wrong. Declaring bf16 for both would have under-declared candle; declaring f32 for both would have over-declared mlx. MLX lane: bf16, the checkpoint's store dtype. The candle sibling row declares f32 for the same component because candle-gen widens it — see that row."
      }
    },
    {
      "model": "sensenova_u1_8b",
      "component": "transformerHead",
      "residentTier": "f32",
      "appliesToTiers": [
        "q4",
        "q8"
      ],
      "backends": [
        "candle"
      ],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "The Qwen3 backbone is packed but the token embedding, `lm_head` and the flow-matching `fm_head` stay dense in every tier, and candle-gen loads the flow-matching `fm_head` at **f32** regardless of the backbone's store dtype, so the component's resident precision on this lane is f32. (the base entry.)",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costBytesByTier": {
          "q4": 2606788608,
          "q8": 2606788608
        },
        "source": "crates/media/candle-gen/candle-gen-sensenova/src/fm.rs:15-25 — the FM head loads \"shapelessly and **at f32** regardless of the backbone's store dtype\" via `crate::quant::get_f32` (sc-14249); crates/media/candle-gen/candle-gen-sensenova/src/quant.rs:92-102 — `get_f32` reads \"at **f32** regardless of the VarBuilder's store dtype\"; the same file's \"Everything else stays dense bf16 in every tier: the token embedding, `lm_head`, ...\" covers `embed_tokens` / `lm_head`, which ride the bf16 store.; isolated artifact: SceneWorks/sensenova-u1-8b-mlx@b6206ea2e888198418b92f3bed31f5506c6183f9:q8/model.safetensors#{language_model.model.embed_tokens,language_model.lm_head,fm_modules.fm_head}.*",
        "isolation": "Summed the exact safetensors-header tensor shapes for q8/model.safetensors#{language_model.model.embed_tokens,language_model.lm_head,fm_modules.fm_head}.* at immutable revision b6206ea2e888198418b92f3bed31f5506c6183f9; 1,244,659,712 embed_tokens/lm_head elements were counted at BF16 and 29,367,296 fm_head elements at F32, matching the Candle load sites. This is isolated mixed-precision weight residency, excluding activations and allocator overhead.",
        "triageDecision": "measure",
        "reviewedCause": "packing-exception",
        "triageNote": "Measure, not eliminate: the provider deliberately excludes this component from packing, and the tree contains no verified quality-neutral lower-tier artifact that could replace it before calibration.",
        "note": "ADDED by the sc-15799 review, which found all six SenseNova-U1 entries undeclared. ADJUDICATION: U1 is a unified MoT model with \"no separate VAE or text encoder\", so the ledger's diffusion vocabulary does not map cleanly — but that is a naming problem, not a reason to omit. The dense matmul targets ARE declarable under this file's threshold (they are `[out, in]` Linears a packer could take, and the packer deliberately skips them), so they are declared: `transformerHead` for `embed_tokens` / `lm_head` / `fm_head`, `visionTower` for the two Conv vision embedders. The dense RMSNorms, QK-norms and timestep/noise-scale embedders are NOT declared — they are per-channel vectors, which the threshold excludes for every model. MEASURED by sc-16015 from the exact selected tensor shapes in each immutable q8 safetensors header, counted at the lane-specific runtime dtype; no whole-model figure or shape estimate is borrowed. SPLIT PER LANE by the second sc-15799 review, which found the single both-lanes row UNDER-DECLARED candle. The two ports make independent dtype decisions and the ledger's uniqueness key is now (model, component, lane), so each lane states its own residentTier instead of one of them being wrong. Declaring bf16 for both would have under-declared candle; declaring f32 for both would have over-declared mlx. CANDLE lane: f32, because `fm_head` is widened by `quant::get_f32`. `embed_tokens` and `lm_head` ride the bf16 store dtype on this lane, so f32 is the component's UPPER resident precision — the tier the row must declare, since the invariant is one-directional about being ABOVE the selected tier. The mlx sibling row declares bf16."
      }
